\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Untied heads, shared gradients, and checkpoint forecasts}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{ledger}

\p{For DGG, the untied head identity and its finite-batch Jensen bound in
\ref{ftip-007Z} and \ref{ftip-0081} differ from an intermediate-occurrence
bound. A shared intermediate weight requires the sum over all
occurrences in \ref{ftip-007Z}; the source's local hypotheses do not establish
its claimed total-gradient bound in
\citet{Section 4.2.1, Lemma 1, Theorem 1, and Appendix A.3}{miao2026when}.
The cancellation example \ref{ftip-0084}
also separates the active clipping interval from the raw-surrogate extension.}

\p{NExt's empirical checkpoint forecasts in
\citet{Sections 3.2, 4.1--4.3, and 5.1}{chen2026lowrank} do not establish a
universal subspace-collapse, capability, or speed theorem. The spectral and
evaluation quantities in \ref{ftip-0086} through \ref{ftip-008B} measure
different trajectory properties.}
